<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Apple's privacy manifest, required for App Store submission.

  The music never leaves the phone: scanning, tags, artwork, shelves, the
  queue and playback all happen on the device. The Apple Watch app talks only
  to the paired iPhone (WatchConnectivity) and sends nothing anywhere else.

  Updated 2026-11-21: the phone app recognises a suite sign-in. It was "Data
  Not Collected" until then. The phone app has no sign-in of its own and
  sends no "the app was opened" event (<UsageTracker /> is mounted on the
  website only, src/App.tsx), but when the phone already holds a UNI·SIM
  session that ANOTHER suite app made (the shared Keychain group
  co.uk.unisim.suite on iOS, the suite's shared sign-in on Android), it reads
  and follows it (src/main.tsx: `noAccounts` is set for the Windows app
  only). Then:

  - Name, linked, App Functionality: the title becomes "Bradley's Jukebox"
    from the account's "Call me" (the SDK's useCallMe: Global Tuning's Call
    me, else the profile's name, else a name-shaped email), and Tune this
    app's name box edits that "Call me" on the account (`suite-call-me` row;
    src/components/Settings.tsx, src/lib/jukeboxTitle.ts). A name typed while
    signed out can seed an account that has none.
  - Email Address, linked, App Functionality: Tune this app ▸ Your Universal
    ID shows the account's email, and the name can fall back to it.
  - User ID, linked, App Functionality: the account id the session carries,
    which keys the reads and writes.
  - Other Data Types, linked, App Functionality: Tune this app's settings
    follow the account (src/stores/settingsStore.ts, the SDK's
    createSyncedSettings, `tune-app:jukebox` row; the colour scheme, language
    and default views in `tune:jukebox` and `suite`; the App name choice in
    `jukebox`). Device-only settings (volume, the typed owner name and the
    rest of `DEVICE_ONLY`) stay on the phone. None of it names a song, an
    artist or a file.

  The suite user count (an install id every 45 s) was retired in
  @unisim/sdk 0.187.0, and the anonymous daily open count is off everywhere
  (src/main.tsx `openCount: false`), so no install id and no count.

  Two lookups send a song's artist and title (never the file) straight from
  the phone to a public service, only when the user asks for what they return:
  Wikipedia for "About this track", and the iTunes Search API for a cover on
  the Requests shelf. None of it reaches our servers or is kept against the
  user, and each request is answered there and then, so under Apple's
  definition it is not collected and is not declared below.

  There is NO online lyrics lookup on iPhone or iPad: `barsOnlineLyrics()`
  (src/lib/nativeFile.ts) is true in the iOS shell, so lyricsStore never lets
  lib/lrclib.ts reach LRCLIB there, and the Tune this app option is hidden.
  Lyrics come only from files on the device and the Apple Music library. The
  LRCLIB lookup exists on the web, desktop and Android only (Android answers
  for it in store-assets/data-safety.json).

  Nothing is used for tracking, and there are no third-party analytics or
  advertising SDKs.

  Required-reason APIs:
  - UserDefaults: MusicFolderPlugin keeps the security-scoped bookmarks of the
    folders the user picked, read only by this app. CA92.1.
  - File timestamps: MusicFolderPlugin reads the modification date of files in
    the folders the user picked, to rescan only what changed (3B52.1).
    AppleMusicPlugin and @capacitor/filesystem read and set dates on copies in
    the app's own container (C617.1). Neither pod ships a manifest; Capacitor's
    core frameworks carry their own.

  Keep this in step with the App Store Connect privacy answers (Name, Email
  Address, User ID, Other Data Types: linked, not tracking, App
  Functionality) and store-assets/data-safety.json.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>3B52.1</string>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<!-- Only with a suite session another app made on the phone. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- "Call me": the title, and Tune's name box. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeName</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Shown in Tune ▸ Your Universal ID. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeEmailAddress</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- The account id the session carries. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeUserID</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- Tune this app settings kept with the account. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherDataTypes</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
